   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# KUBA_Regions From Illustrator\n\n1. `ai_file`: the project .ai (saved PDF compatible, Illustrator's default) or a PDF. Hidden layers are read too.\n2. Matrix: any image of the matrix size (the artboard must have the same aspect; one uniform scale).\n3. Roles are guessed per layer (see the report): stroke layers = **lines** (cells between the lines), filled layers = **shapes** (on top), a MASK/range layer touching the border = **outside**, a full background fill / text / `_` layers = **ignore**, image layers = **reference**.\n4. Override in `layer_roles`, e.g. `MASK = outside`, `CENTRE, COUR, JAR = lines`, `FLOOR_* = tag`.\n5. Cells are named `<LAYER>_001..`, grouped by shape (`<LAYER>_g137` = the repeated windows) and tagged with the layer: rules `[tag:COUR]`, `[group:CENTRE_g137]`.\n\n\n"
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
